.TH CLOCK_GETTIME 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
clock_gettime \- Linux x86-64 syscall 228
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/syscall_220_259.h>
.B int clock_gettime(int clock, struct timespec* value);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads a clock using the Linux syscall.
This is a direct Linux x86-64 syscall wrapper; availability and permissions depend on the kernel and security policy.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the syscall result, or \-1 with errno set on failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR clock_gettime (2)
